# Backend Docker build context exclusions (DEVIATIONS.md #45a).
#
# Without this file, `COPY . .` in the Dockerfile pulls in whatever happens
# to exist locally under backend/ — including a local .venv, which is
# exactly what happened here: a `python -m venv .venv` created per this
# repo's own README ballooned a `docker build` from ~6.5GB to ~19GB because
# nothing told Docker to skip it.
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/
.git/
# Bind-mounted into `api` at /app/results (DEVIATIONS.md #270); a full
# ablation run is GBs and doesn't belong in the image.
results/
